# pyron COSMO DISRUPTION — THE MAINTAINER'S 100% REPRO (14z-75).
#
# Reported reproducing on BOTH MAME and FBNeo: 41236 + 2K, and then HOLD
# until the move finishes BY ITSELF. The energy sphere that does the hits
# appears for a few frames and the game CRASH-RESETS, with or without the
# sphere connecting.
#
# WHY THE EARLIER RIGS MISSED IT. Replay 71 and replay 77 both RELEASE the
# pair after ~41 frames (3415-3455). That aborts the move before it
# completes, so the sphere phase is never reached — 77 fired the EX four
# times over twelve attempts and never crashed. The hold length IS the
# repro condition, not the motion.
#
# So: ONE attempt, 2K held for 400 frames and never released inside the
# window, then a long tail so a watchdog reset has somewhere to show.
#
# THE MOVE COSTS A STOCK — with an empty meter the pair is downgraded to a
# single button and nothing fires. Run with:
#   POKES="1400:ff8782:11;1450:ff8782:11;1500:ff8782:11;3000:ff8509:09;3300:ff8509:09"
#
# VERDICT: a watchdog reset is not a 68k exception. Judge by whether the
# match SURVIVES — P1 +0x382 still 0x11 late in the run — or by snapshots.
300-305 sys=C1
800-803 sys=S1
1700-1702 p1=1
# 41236, then HOLD 2K and do not let go
3400-3402 p1=L
3403-3405 p1=DL
3406-3408 p1=D
3409-3411 p1=DR
3412-3414 p1=R
3415-3815 p1=45
5200 wait
